## Summary

I found and fixed the off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The bug was using `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]` to return the first word. This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail: returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error: IndexError when trying to access index 1 of a single-element list

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`. All tests now pass successfully.
